{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וזכרת כי עבד היית במצרים", :translit "u'zkharta ki eved hayita b'mitzrayim", :gloss "and you shall remember that you were a slave in Egypt"} {:he "לא תחבול", :translit "lo tachbol", :gloss "you shall not take a pledge"} {:he "ונתתי לך חן בעיני מצרים", :translit "v'natati l'cha chen b'einei mitzrayim", :gloss "and I granted you favor in the eyes of the Egyptians"} {:he "ושאלו לך כלי כסף וכלי זהב ושמלות", :translit "v'sha'alu l'chli kessef u'chli zahav u'simlot", :gloss "and they lent you silver vessels and gold vessels and garments"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Thematic link between the exodus memory of receiving pledged goods and the prohibition of taking pledges"}], :frame {:text "Exodus 12:35-36 records that the Israelites asked the Egyptians for silver vessels, gold vessels, and garments, and that God granted the people favor in the Egyptians' eyes so they gave them. Ba'al HaTurim reads the command to remember Egyptian slavery here in Deuteronomy 24:18 as pointing back to that borrowing: just as the Israelites received items from the Egyptians, they must not oppress a fellow Israelite by taking pledges.", :sources ["Exodus 12:35-36" "Deuteronomy 24:17"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Thematic link between the exodus memory of receiving pledged goods and the prohibition of taking pledges", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:38:56.968114124Z", :model "glm-5.2"}